. 
.         * NOTE: When we performed our analysis for H1 we conducted a series o
> f robustness checks to examine whether having "at least one daughter" (d_daug
> hter) influences attitudes towards gender equality (plh0395avg) with differen
> t specifications. We noted that the estimates for d_daughter are always signi
> ficant except when we include the variable log_pglabgro, which stands for the
>  current net labor income. If this variable is omitted or replaced by the mon
> thly household net income (hghinc) the estimates for d_daughter become negati
> ve and significantly different from 0 (p-values < 0.05). 
. 
. * EXTRACT AND EXPORT RESULTS * 
. 
.         * Extract the required statistics
. 
.                 * (i) coefficient estimate
.                 local coefficient = _b[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (ii) standard error
.                 local se = _se[d_daughter]

. 
.                 * (iii) family of the test statistic (e.g. z, t, F, Chi²)
.                 local test_stat_family = "t"

. 
.                 * (iv) residual and model degrees of freedom (DFs) if applica
> ble
.                 local df_residual = e(df_r)

.                 local df_model = e(df_m)

. 
.                 * (v) p-value
.                 local p_value = _b[d_daughter] / _se[d_daughter]

.                 local p_value = 2 * ttail(e(df_r), abs(`p_value'))

. 
.                 * (vi) number of observations
.                 local num_obs = e(N)

. 
.                 * (vii) number of participants
.                 quietly levelsof pid if e(sample), local(participants)

.                 local num_participants : word count `participants'

. 
.                 * (viii) interpretation of directionality
.                 local interpretation "positive coeffiecient is in line with h
> ypothesis"

.                 
.         // Display the saved statistics
.         di "Coefficient: `coefficient'"
Coefficient: .1830022896812752

.         di "Standard Error: `se'"
Standard Error: .1245007343168517

.         di "Test Statistic Family: `test_stat_family'"
